			"text": "Typical Stats from the package record: ST 13, DX 14, IQ 11, HT 11, HP 15, WILL 13, PER 12, FP 11, SPEED 6.25, MOVE 6, DODGE 9, DR 1. GCS derives its own values by applying the ancestry; where the two differ, the package's Typical Stats are what the Dungeons on Automatic encounter tables use."
		},
		{
			"id": "nlAl-SKGN2ab2k9hM",
			"text": "Encounter rating: CER 29 (offense 17, protection 12), threat tier standard, appearing 1."
		},
		{
			"id": "nWRvpP1DMZp5P5dlv",
			"text": "Petrifying Gaze: No attack roll and no active defense. Petrifying Gaze (15): 1d-4 toxic, Reach Ranged, gaze. Meet the eyes and resist with HT, or stiffen by degrees into stone. The fiendish blood has not changed the family gift, only the patience with which it is used."
		},
		{
			"id": "nIu-9DT8zJd0-iOZC",
			"text": "GCS ancestry draft: gcs/half-fiend-medusa.gct"
		},
		{
			"id": "nX8WbUpyEdU1lpWPI",
			"text": "Independent build total: 234 points of racial traits plus 18 points of racial skills."
		},
		{
			"id": "nC_OY--ucl3mijtyf",
			"text": "Answers the SRD heading(s): Half-Fiend (SRD 3.5). Only the creature identity is taken from the SRD; the GURPS statistics, ratings and prose are this project's own work and reproduce no SRD text."
		},
		{
			"id": "nwgFJ8jeivYEgTeIm",
			"text": "Typical Stats, damage and ratings are derived from the racial template, not authored beside it, so the sheet and the stat block cannot disagree."
		},
		{
			"id": "nNSpOO31ZoZVOniYV",
			"text": "Body mass used to scale this build: 70 kg. ST, Size Modifier and DR are checked against it; see the gurps-animal-sanity-check skill for the bands."
		},
		{
			"id": "nwf0KAVg5ydA4RiOq",
			"text": "Movement: ground Move 6 (primary); air Move 12. The published Move is the primary medium's cruising Move; sprint figures are stated here and not folded into it."
		},
		{
			"id": "ntbP82k7gKa7nftpo",
			"text": "Treasure and grappling are not authored for this batch and ship as explicit nulls; `lair` carries a short habitat note, because where a wandering animal dens is an encounter fact rather than a loot one."
		},
		{
			"id": "n0Ve7HIk2MI9I5B3C",
			"text": "The base creature is the library's Medusa; the fiendish half adds wings, fire resistance, claws, and intent. The gaze is priced through the affliction term exactly as the base medusa's is."
		},
		{
			"id": "nDQDm3JUzeuZvkGIa",
			"text": "It answers the SRD's Half-Fiend template heading as the sample that page prints."
		},
